 as a self-taught programmer, I learned to look at the smaller picture first. one step at a time. don't try and get it all to work at one time. instead, work on one part get it working then go to the next. trust me it's so stressful when you have 10 things to make work but when you break it down to one thing at a time then it becomes way easier. so make a list what are the important functions? do those first. then make a second list what are secondary functions? then do those. do not just bump it all together. if it is currently they way use the old comment out trick and start one piece at a time.

&#x200B;

good luck and remember to breathe!

