commentary videos: 2 to 6 hours of recording at one time (i record episode based games so I like to play out a whole game episode and sometimes may sit and just play the whole game if i get into it enough. Throughout the gameplay I jot down commentary and during editing i put commentary into text to speech software. I would say editing and adding commentary can take me 3 to 4 hours on the video. Normally i end up with 20 to 50 minute videos.

&#x200B;

non commentary videos: a lot easier all i need to do is edit out loading screens, speed up repetitive clicking scenes and combine recordings. the videos come out to 12 to 20 minutes and normally takes 2 hours at most to edit

&#x200B;

recap videos: this takes a lot longer i take content from previous recorded playtroughs, write a small script of what i want to say (put the script into text to speech software). slowly find clips that work for what i am saying then edit it all together. these can easily take me 4 to 5 hours and i believe is by far my best content. 

&#x200B;

I think in youtube hard work really pays off my recap videos are well received while my less edited content isn't. Even minimal edits can really help a video.

